identifier: NCIT:C80300
preferred_term: D-Maltose monohydrate
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: NCIT:C80300
  ontology_label: Maltose Monohydrate
  ontology_source: NCIT
  mapping_quality: CAS_RN_LOOKUP
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureBotHT
    notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 6363-53-7 present, but no CHEBI entry
      exists for the monohydrate specifically (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem
      CID synonyms). FEBA/Hans80 panels: FEBA_carbon. Used in 9 CultureBot media;
      samples: Mega, ZMB Gut, SGW Northen Exometabolite mix 5x…. Curator can promote
      to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds D-maltose monohydrate.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_REVIEW
    source: family_mismatch_fix
    notes: 'fix(family-mismatch): was CHEBI:233428 (5-(N-ethyl-N-isopropyl) amiloride)
      from a stale pubchem-xref hit on PubChem CID 23615261; the bogus CHEBI was removed
      from the published SSSOM in PR #2 / commit 887ee9f and the ontology_mapping
      is now retargeted at CHEBI:17306 (maltose) as the correct narrowMatch parent.
      D-Maltose monohydrate is a hydrate of D-maltose, which has no separate CHEBI;
      maltose (CHEBI:17306) is the closest available parent.'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:17306 (''maltose'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files
      hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'Resolve #1117 for this owner to NCIT:C80300, Maltose Monohydrate, using
      CAS_RN_LOOKUP as method provenance. The archived catalogue explicitly selects
      SigmaM5885/CAS6363-53-7/360.31; the inspected official M5885 specification confirms
      CAS and C12H22O11·H2O. NCIt links this CAS to UNIIDM477EE40D; the GSRS PRIMARY
      record explicitly cross-links C80300, CAS6363-53-7, D-(+)-MALTOSE MONOHYDRATE
      and beta naming, and PubChem23615261. The open-chain representation and beta
      synonym occur in that same registry identity; §3 readability/orderability supports
      the readable monohydrate node, without choosing a different anomer from lexical
      resemblance. Keep generic Maltose_Hydrate separate. See the complete identity,
      mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/D-Maltose_Monohydrate.yaml. Primary source
      references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C80300?include=full;
      https://gsrs.ncats.nih.gov/api/v1/substances/DM477EE40D?view=full; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/23615261/property/MolecularFormula,InChI,InChIKey/JSON;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/6363-53-7/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON;
      https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/specification-sheets/677/787/M5885-BULK________SIAL_____.pdf.
      Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
